{SECT 0 {EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 44 "Darboux.mws: Examples of D
arboux curves from" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 94 "                   \+
     F.Ulmer & J.A.Weil, Note on Kovacic's Algorithm, JSC 22, 179-200,
 1996" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 258 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 16 "IMPORTANT: the  " }
{TEXT 257 8 "bernina " }{TEXT -1 66 " executable must be in your path \+
before you can execute this demo." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
50 "To start, we tell maple about the location of the " }{TEXT 258 9 "
bernina.m" }{TEXT -1 31 " file, which is located in the " }{TEXT 259 
5 "maple" }{TEXT -1 140 " directory of bernina.\n Replace the '.' by t
he appropriate directory on your system. The following line is only va
lid if you are using maple" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 10 "from the  \+
" }{TEXT 256 5 "maple" }{TEXT -1 106 "  directory of bernina. Alternat
ively, you can add a line to this effect in your .mapleinit file, and \+
then" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 24 "run maple from anywhere." }}
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 32 "restart; libname := `.`,libname:" }
}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 78 "We then load the bernina interfa
ce, bringing the bernina functions into scope:" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 14 "with(bernina);" }}{PARA 12 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#7:%
(DarbouxG%&LoewyG%(adjointG%&applyG%*decomposeG%(dfactorG%*eigenringG%
5exponentialSolutionsG%.exteriorPowerG%(leftGcdG%(leftLcmG%-makeIntegr
alG%%multG%*normalizeG%1polynomialKernelG%3polynomialSolutionG%1radica
lSolutionsG%/rationalKernelG%1rationalSolutionG%)rightGcdG%)rightLcmG%
.rightQuotientG%0symmetricKernelG%/symmetricPowerG" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 
"" 0 "" {TEXT -1 177 "We first define a short verification function fo
r proposed solutions of 2nd order operators (yes, both calls to simpli
fy and normal seem to be necessary for the examples below)." }}{PARA 
0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 202 "verify := proc(L, D, x, solutions) local
 i; seq(simplify(normal(coeff(L,D,2) * diff(solutions[i],x$2) + coeff(
L,D,1) * diff(solutions[i],x) + coeff(L,D,0) * solutions[i])), i = 1..
nops(solutions)); end;" }}{PARA 12 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%'verifyGR6
&%\"LG%\"DG%\"xG%*solutionsG6#%\"iG6\"F--%$seqG6$-%)simplifyG6#-%'norm
alG6#,(*&-%&coeffG6%9$9%\"\"#\"\"\"-%%diffG6$&9'6#8$-%\"$G6$9&F>F?F?*&
-F:6%F<F=F?F?-FA6$FCFJF?F?*&-F:6%F<F=\"\"!F?FCF?F?/FF;F?-%%nopsG6#FDF-
F-F-" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 46 "First a  with a completel
y reducible operator:" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 20 "L := D^2 +
 3/16/x^2;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"LG,&*$)%\"DG\"\"#\"
\"\"\"\"\"*&F*F**$)%\"xG\"\"#F*!\"\"#\"\"$\"#;" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> \+
